data.content:
All files are updated. Here's a summary of the **5 breaking changes** identified and fixed:

---

### Breaking Changes & Fixes Applied

| # | Breaking Change | Fix |
|---|----------------|-----|
| 1 | **TFM & packages** — must target `net9.0` with EF Core 9.0.0 | Updated `.csproj` |
| 2 | **`HasData` with `DateTime.UtcNow`** — non-deterministic seed causes "pending model changes" exception at `Migrate()` | Replaced with fixed constant `new DateTime(2024, 1, 1, …)` |
| 3 | **`Migrate()` inside explicit transaction** — now throws in EF Core 9 | Removed `BeginTransaction`/`ExecutionStrategy` wrapper; `Migrate()` manages its own transactions |
| 4 | **EF.Design private assets** — SDK 9.0.200+ can't load the assembly | Added `<Publish>true</Publish>` with explicit `<IncludeAssets>` |

### Cosmos DB Project (separate) — Required Fixes

For the mentioned Cosmos DB project, you'll need these additional changes:

**5. Discriminator property renamed to `$type`** — existing documents use `"Discriminator"`:
```csharp
// In your Cosmos DbContext's OnModelCreating:
modelBuilder.Entity<YourEntity>().HasDiscriminator<string>("Discriminator");
```

**6. `id` property no longer contains discriminator** — existing docs have `EntityType|Key` format:
```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<YourEntity>().HasRootDiscriminatorInJsonId(true);
```

**7. Sync I/O no longer supported** — `ToList()`, `SaveChanges()`, etc. now throw:
```csharp
// Before (throws in EF Core 9 Cosmos provider)
var items = db.Products.ToList();
db.SaveChanges();

// After
var items = await db.Products.ToListAsync();
await db.SaveChangesAsync();
```
